<p>For folks who like using the development build of Emacs (at the time of this writing Emacs 31.0.5) on macOS, it turns out there is a <a href="https://github.com/kickingvegas/scrim/issues/76">bug</a> in how <a href="http://yummymelon.com/scrim/">Scrim</a> sends Org protocol requests to it.</p>
<p>A fix has been identified and so far it works fine for both Emacs 30.2 and 31.0.5 from my testing. That said, it is always better to have more folks trying it out.</p>
<p>If you use the latest Emacs 31.0.5+ on macOS and use (or are interested in using) Org protocol, I invite you to <a href="https://testflight.apple.com/join/5HNzNtft">try out a TestFlight build of Scrim v1.1.3</a>.</p>
<p>If this is the first time you’ve heard about Scrim, learn more about it at <a href="http://yummymelon.com/scrim/">http://yummymelon.com/scrim/</a></p>
<p>Thanks much!</p>